  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Olmesartan is an angiotensin II receptor blocker used to treat high blood pressure (arterial hypertension) and has also been used for congestive heart failure. It is an approved medicine, available alone and in fixed combinations with diuretics or calcium channel blockers, and is widely used as an antihypertensive.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421156\">Wikidata Q421156</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>olmesartan medoxomil</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>C09CA08</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00275\">DB00275</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/158781\">158781</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:48416\">48416</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q421156\">Q421156</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C24H26N6O3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>446.511 g/mol (PubChem CID 158781)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>3.8 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table><p><small>Drugs.Common 25.09 gave 558.6 g/mol (+25.1 %); replaced by the value above</small></p></body></html>"));
